From 1c19444f84f279aaefe6c8f4584471a3ded12ddb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ecogamezz <33791269+ecogamezz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:57:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] WowCraft: login from Minecraft, collision, the overlay,
 blocks and bodies

- account: the WoW account comes from Minecraft's world
  (WOWCRAFT_ACCOUNT_FILE), behind WowCraft's wait dialog.
- collision: every static collider the body walks on streams to Minecraft
  in 8-block regions (exact triangles, then 1/8-block voxels with the land
  filled two blocks deep), from a voxelizer thread, nearest first.
- overlay: Minecraft's hotbar, hearts, hand and screens as one quad over
  WoW's interface in the player-UI pass.
- blocks: Minecraft's block sections, our Minecraft body and its scene as
  meshes in our world, lit by Minecraft's own light levels.

Verified live: a stand-in Minecraft received 847 regions and stood on
Northshire's ground; its blocks and overlay showed in the client.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
